{"id": "EUVD-2026-28580", "enisaUuid": "6126817c-3300-36d3-93cf-3ac35d5a5ed8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: verisilicon: Avoid G2 bus error while decoding H.264 and HEVC\n\nFor the i.MX8MQ platform, there is a hardware limitation: the g1 VPU and\ng2 VPU cannot decode simultaneously; otherwise, it will cause below bus\nerror and produce corrupted pictures, even potentially lead to system hang.\n\n[  110.527986] hantro-vpu 38310000.video-codec: frame decode timed out.\n[  110.583517] hantro-vpu 38310000.video-codec: bus error detected.\n\nTherefore, it is necessary to ensure that g1 and g2 operate alternately.\nThis allows for successful multi-instance decoding of H.264 and HEVC.\n\nTo achieve this, g1 and g2 share the same v4l2_m2m_dev, and then the\nv4l2_m2m_dev can handle the scheduling.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T13:11:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:35", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f988fbf0536b42f6a05ccc1ac709d60236ec1aa6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2efc1e8ab65bdb9b892af132887323e4df92f02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5133ef7c893c2c3aee7dd12503dc480de9dbfbb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/286d629d10640bc22f3bf46aa4f356eb7975e862", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0203ddf9af7c8e170e1e99ce83b4dc07f0cd765"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-43310", "GHSA-6g88-27p6-cw4p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "195b3484-8beb-3bc0-873a-82c824dc5184", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb5dd5a0fa518dff14ff2b90837c3c8f98f4dd5c <f988fbf0536b42f6a05ccc1ac709d60236ec1aa6"}, {"id": "32a71706-8559-39e4-bee7-270d29c16539", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "3d4e1346-06ee-3750-8a6a-d4664ac9f049", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb5dd5a0fa518dff14ff2b90837c3c8f98f4dd5c <286d629d10640bc22f3bf46aa4f356eb7975e862"}, {"id": "41e0e441-74ec-3ded-a694-4b9917af08b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5fe56e10-9273-3b0d-9520-78c61e4a0b7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "68e548ad-0284-392e-9649-9518e2459132", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "70161c0c-4033-3040-8f89-42ee0261f2f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "88772ba5-d10c-3cd9-a5f8-7e23a9909889", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "b18833d3-7c64-37e5-8060-e6dd77e2e5bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb5dd5a0fa518dff14ff2b90837c3c8f98f4dd5c <5133ef7c893c2c3aee7dd12503dc480de9dbfbb5"}, {"id": "e6000249-d6e9-305e-848b-6fae33b19c4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb5dd5a0fa518dff14ff2b90837c3c8f98f4dd5c <e0203ddf9af7c8e170e1e99ce83b4dc07f0cd765"}, {"id": "f275c46c-befb-3331-92a8-e0238496b956", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb5dd5a0fa518dff14ff2b90837c3c8f98f4dd5c <f2efc1e8ab65bdb9b892af132887323e4df92f02"}, {"id": "f3d91a9b-922a-3307-b053-cee0b2cfd528", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5228c529-92ac-3c7b-9e31-a15f001a690c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}